[36m(main_task pid=2937563)[0m <think>As I have found information on the long service leave in the 1860s in Australia, I will now answer the remaining question about the visa requirements for Australian citizens traveling to Canada.</think>
[36m(main_task pid=2937563)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2937563)[0m <answer>Visa requirements for Australian citizens traveling to Canada: Australian citizens generally do not need a visa to enter Canada for stays of up to six months. However, they do need to obtain an eTA (Electronic Travel Authorization) before arrival to air, land, or sea ports. The eTA allows stays of up to 90 days in Canada for tourism, business, or medical purposes. If the intended stay exceeds six months, or the purpose of the stay is for study or work, a visa is required.</answer>
